  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Laid out as three columns (Japanese unit / English equivalent / French equivalent) under five centred sub-headings; each sub-heading made a part. Brace groups (Koku, Kwan, Kin, Momme) joined with '; ' in one cell.",
   "Square ri: last digit of the cho figure is damaged (reads like '3' but the glyph is broken and could be 5 or 6); written as '129[?]'.",
   "Cho row: '2.45064 acres' — the digit after '450' is slightly broken but reads as 6.",
   "Moneys: sterling figure printed as '2ˢ 0ᵈ·581' (superscript s/d, raised point); transcribed as '2s. 0d.581'.",
   "Moneys: marks figure printed '2 0924' — no decimal point visible in the scan; transcribed as seen. The '(Ger.)' has a malformed opening parenthesis in print.",
   "'Tsubo or bu' is followed in print by a stray mark/dash; no equals-figure in the English column for Ko (Formosa) or Go.",
   "Momme=10 fun: 'f' of fun is faint.",
   "No totals printed."
  ],
